{
  "version": "v1",
  "description": "Dialer cursor rules. Input: an optional seeded or recorded position (`seed`), whether this connect is a reconnect, the link kind (`stream` with its ack's `stream` info and optional `resume` outcome, or `legacy`: a plain ack or no handshake), then a sequence of frames: `event` (the raw JSON offset token of an event frame, null for a missing one), `reset` and `position` control frames. Output: the link-up result (`resume` as reported in link.connected, and the invalidation published before anything else, if any), one result per frame (`deliver`, `drop` for a duplicate, `ok` for a position, an `invalidated` object, or `protocol_error`, after which the link is closed and no frames follow), and the final position (null when none is held). A resume is wanted when a position is held or the connect is a reconnect; a link that comes up without `replaying` while a resume is wanted invalidates. Reset (ack or frame) sets the position to (stream, head); position frames apply max; duplicates are offsets <= the position; reset or position naming another stream is a protocol error; a legacy link clears the position. Invalidation payload offsets are decimal strings, empty for `unsupported`. A `replaying` ack for a stream other than the held position's is treated as a reset with reason `stream`. A reset frame whose head is below the position is a protocol error (offsets only grow).",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "fresh stream connect starts at the head",
      "seed": null,
      "reconnect": false,
      "link": "stream",
      "ack": {
        "stream": {
          "id": "S",
          "oldest": "1",
          "head": "10"
        }
      },
      "frames": [
        {
          "event": "11"
        },
        {
          "event": "12"
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "link_up": {
          "resume": "none",
          "invalidated": null
        },
        "frames": [
          "deliver",
          "deliver"
        ],
        "position": {
          "stream": "S",
          "offset": "12"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "replay drops duplicates and accepts filtered holes",
